@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About SOMA";
}

<h1 class="display-5 mb-3">About SOMA</h1>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">The Setting</h2>
    <p>
        Set in the year 2104, SOMA follows Simon Jarrett, who mysteriously awakens in PATHOS-II,
        an isolated and decaying underwater research station. Simon had undergone a brain scan in 2015,
        only to "wake up" nearly a century later in a mechanical body.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">The Gameplay</h2>
    <p>
        The game has no combat system. Players rely entirely on stealth, environmental awareness,
        and puzzle-solving to evade corrupted machines and hostile biomechanical creatures.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">The Story</h2>
    <p>
        The rogue AI of the PATHOS-II facility, the WAU, operates on a distorted mandate to preserve
        humanity at all costs. The result is grotesque cyborgs and digital echoes of people trapped in
        perpetual agony.
    </p>
    <p>
        Simon and his companion Catherine work to launch the ARK, a digital utopia containing the last
        preserved human minds, into space. Along the way the narrative dismantles the illusion of
        continuous existence.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">The Themes</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Artificial intelligence</li>
        <li>Identity and consciousness</li>
        <li>The "ship of Theseus" paradox</li>
        <li>What it truly means to be human</li>
    </ul>
</section>
